{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:2f144b9083641713","name":"U-LAV","source":{"id":"source:reference-2f144b9083641713","title":"U-LAV","revision":20809,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T00:33:45Z","sha256":"84745cea56e242188ad436114e2b76e0d304a82ecb10213b4ece328e6cc6f73d","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20809","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=U-LAV&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-2f144b9083641713","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rebellion Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rebellion_Era_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Republic","referenceId":"reference:332055cafc4223eb"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Rebel Alliance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Rebel_Alliance","referenceId":"reference:52c543ff6d31425c"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Sienar Ultra-Light Assault Vehicles are small, fast, and extremely agile ",{"tag":"a","children":["Landspeeders"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Landspeeders"}," designed for rapid deployment and quick, slashing strikes across the battlefield. The U-LAV's size makes it ideal for deployment from drop ships or large transports. During ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"},", U-LAVs are highly effective at piercing the lines of CIS Droid units. Zipping through the Droid formations, the U-LAV's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gunner"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gunner","referenceId":"reference:0cbc0bc5729f801f"}," has ample targets for the Double ",{"tag":"a","children":["Laser Cannon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Laser_Cannon","referenceId":"reference:0911ab4bc0e93386"}," and, after breaking through the line, the advantage of the more powerful rear-facing ",{"tag":"a","children":["Blaster Cannon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Blaster_Cannon","referenceId":"reference:ae1584087cb7657b"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The early Empire regularly used U-LAVs, but soon replaced them with larger and more powerful ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"}," with forward-facing primary weapons. Most U-LAVs were left forgotten in Imperial surplus depots, too small to attract buyers. Decades later, a Rebel commando raid steals a huge fleet of U-LAVs from a minimally guarded Imperial storage facility on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hiffis"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hiffis?action=edit&redlink=1"},". Rebel technicians make a few updates and modifications- including the addition of light shielding- and put the durable old U-LAVs into service throughout the galaxy. Though hindered by their rear-facing weaponry and half-meter flight ceiling, the U-LAVs are a welcome addition to the Vehicle-starved Rebels.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Skilled)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["U-LAV Statistics (CL 5)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Huge ",{"tag":"a","children":["Speeder"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Speeder"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +10; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +6\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 17 (",{"tag":"a","child